From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 06:40:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The Remix API: an empty value changes nothing and succeeds,
 as before 0101

Patch 0101 made remixapi_SetConfigVariable return INVALID_ARGUMENTS whenever readOption reported that it read
nothing, to refuse a value that fails to parse. Config::findOption takes an empty value for no value, so readOption
also reports nothing read for "": an empty value had always changed nothing and answered success. The RTX package's
Lua sets its session texture lists and the eye-white aliases to "" whenever they are empty, often (902 times in a
four-minute PoC session), and after 0101 every one of those calls printed a failure in the game's console. An empty
value succeeds again; a value that fails to parse is still refused.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_remix_api.cpp | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_remix_api.cpp b/src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_remix_api.cpp
index a812ea221..c489a7409 100644
--- a/src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_remix_api.cpp
+++ b/src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_remix_api.cpp
@@ -1903,8 +1903,11 @@ namespace {
     newSetting.setOptionMove(std::move(strKey), std::string{ value });
     // NoSave options such as showUI are transient. A User-layer API write would otherwise
     // override the Derived-layer Close/timeout action and leave the menu stuck open.
-    // NV-DXVK start: a value that fails to parse is refused, not thrown through the API (GMod: any server's Lua calls it)
-    if (!option->readOption(newSetting, option->getTargetLayer(dxvk::RtxOptionLayer::getUserLayer()))) {
+    // NV-DXVK start: a value that fails to parse is refused, not thrown through the API (GMod: any server's Lua calls it).
+    // An empty value is no value to Config::findOption, so readOption changes nothing for it: that stays a success, as
+    // it always was (the RTX package's Lua sets its session lists to "" when they are empty, often).
+    const bool emptyValue = value[0] == '\0';
+    if (!option->readOption(newSetting, option->getTargetLayer(dxvk::RtxOptionLayer::getUserLayer())) && !emptyValue) {
       return REMIXAPI_ERROR_CODE_INVALID_ARGUMENTS;
     }
     // NV-DXVK end
